        <h1>LeetCode 3870: Count Commas in Range (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an integer n. Return the total number of commas used when writing every integer
                from 1 to n (inclusive) in standard number formatting, where a comma is placed after every
                three digits counted from the right and numbers with fewer than four digits have no commas.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: n = 1002<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: The numbers 1,000, 1,001, and 1,002 each contribute one comma, for a total of 3.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int countCommas(int limit) {
        long long total = 0;
        long long boundary = 1000;
        while (boundary &lt;= limit) {
            total += limit - boundary + 1;
            boundary *= 1000;
        }
        return static_cast&lt;int&gt;(total);
    }
};</code></pre>
